# ── generated / OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.DS_Store

# ── local machine config, not shared ─────────────────────────────────────
**/.claude/settings.local.json

# ── local working notes ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The tracked CLAUDE.md is the *portable* version, deliberately free of any
# reference to work projects. CLAUDE.local.md is the fuller local copy that
# names them — it stays off the public repo.
CLAUDE.local.md

# ── stale backups: git history replaces these ────────────────────────────
*.backup-*.html

# ── known cruft ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
nightcore/page7.html

# ── third-party media: THIS REPO IS PUBLIC ───────────────────────────────
# The album rip, the nightcore renders derived from it, and the auction-house
# catalogues are all commercial copyrighted material. They are also ~340MB,
# which GitHub would want in Git LFS regardless (the largest PDF is 74MB,
# against a 100MB hard limit per file).
#
# They stay local. Delete a line below if you decide a category is yours to
# publish — but the scripts are all written to read from local paths, so
# nothing here needs them committed to run.
*.mp3
*.wav
*.flac
*.m4a
*.aac
*.pdf

# Song-lyrics corpus — third-party text, same reasoning as above.
drake/drake_data.xls

# The tracked CLAUDE.md *is* this file's content — committing both would be a
# duplicate. Keep it locally as the source you copy from.
CLAUDE-portable.md

# leverage: raw Retrosheet season + the parsed intermediate (both regenerable)
leverage/data/
